// Required example 9: import two aliased time libraries. Both packages are
// named "time"; the aliases are the only thing that make them referenceable
// in the same file, and each keeps its own canonical registry identity.
//
// An activity, not a rule: once Milestone 6 (ADR 0032) made cross-package
// calls real instead of opaque, this calls company.time's addBusinessDays
// — a rule — which only an activity may do (ADR 0029: a rule calls nothing
// at all, the same restriction regardless of which package the callee
// lives in; ADR 0030: that composition is exactly Activity's job).
use company.time as businessTime
use standard.time as systemTime

activity computeFollowUpDate(from: systemTime.Instant) -> systemTime.Instant {
    return businessTime.addBusinessDays(from, 3)
}
